WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.740
I recently graduated.

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.850
Thank you for the congratulations.

3
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:11.090
But I have to admit that it wasn't easy for me right before the end.

4
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:19.640
I had a lot of exams to pass and a lot of books to read.

5
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:34.890
I would lie in bed with my head bursting with information and, of course, instead of getting some sleep, I would pick up my phone and scroll through social media so as not to miss anything.

6
00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:38.530
TikTok took up most of my time.

7
00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:45.310
In a pile of videos with no point whatsoever, I came across something very useful.

8
00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.890
They were videos by Ivana Aćimović.

9
00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:53.430
She is a student at the Faculty of Medicine in Belgrade and the mother of three-year-old Kruna.

10
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:59.880
Judging by her videos, Ivana gets a lot done in 24 hours.

11
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:06.190
She studies, films for TikTok, cooks, is a mom, and even works out.

12
00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:15.770
I would think: if Ivana can take care of a little human and study on top of everything, I have no excuse.

13
00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:20.490
Then, finally, I would put the phone down and replace it with a book.

14
00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.640
You are listening to Diary of a Youth.

15
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.860
An award-winning podcast about the life of young people in Serbia.

16
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.680
My name is Milica Mihajlović.

17
00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:41.650
Finding out she was pregnant filled Ivana with emotions.

18
00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.960
I cried from happiness.

19
00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:51.150
I was also scared, I'm telling you, because I realized what a responsibility that is.

20
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:56.160
At that moment Ivana was enrolling in the third year of medical school.

21
00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:02.490
She was aware that the best thing for her child's future was to continue her studies.

22
00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:08.700
But, as you probably know, there is a lot to study at medical school.

23
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:17.900
The material is enormous and the exams are hard, because in the end you are training to be a doctor, to save human lives tomorrow.

24
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:24.610
And on top of all that, you also have one little life next to you that you constantly have to take care of.

25
00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:31.790
To prepare for her exams, Ivana often had to leave Kruna with her mother.

26
00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:37.310
Kruna was only three months old at the time, and that wasn't easy for Ivana.

27
00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:48.690
There were moments when I would call on video, cry, the tears are coming now, and ask: God, am I a good enough mom, why am I not with her right now?

28
00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:55.230
And to make the situation even more complicated, Kruna's dad was a student until recently too.

29
00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:58.700
And no less than at the law faculty.

30
00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:06.650
Although in recent years he didn't have to go to classes, he had to prepare for exams and work on top of that.

31
00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:12.050
I had to ask Ivana what their life looked like in those moments.

32
00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:20.100
I'm at the faculty, and he usually gets up at five in the morning and studies two or three hours before going to work.

33
00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:31.890
I'm with her, I get her ready when she wakes up, and then when he gets back from work he rests, spends time with her, then I take over again so he can study, and I study then or in the evening.

34
00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:35.730
If his exam period is over, then I study more.

35
00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:41.210
I used the time to study when I wasn't at the faculty or while she's in kindergarten.

36
00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:48.650
On weekends the grandmas want to see her, so she's there for half a day, and then somehow we both sit down and study.

37
00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:54.830
Phew, this pace made my head spin.

38
00:03:55.630 --> 00:04:00.960
So much so that I'll leave Ivana and her family for a moment and hop over to Niš.

39
00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.690
My colleague Katarina is waiting for me there.

40
00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:13.870
She is a journalism student at the Faculty of Philosophy in Niš and the mother of a girl who is not yet a year old at the time of recording this episode.

41
00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:22.230
Katarina is not only a student mom but also the deputy editor of the youth newsroom Pressing in Niš.

42
00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:30.010
On top of that, during her pregnancy Katarina went back to her previous job and worked as a gynecology nurse.

43
00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.550
My head started spinning again.

44
00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:40.230
It seemed to me that the life of student moms is one big carousel.

45
00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:47.870
You know those fairground carousels where a couple holds hands while sitting in neighboring baskets?

46
00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:52.170
Maybe that hand-holding is also a kind of support.

47
00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:57.590
And who holds the hands of young student mothers on this carousel of life?

48
00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:10.640
The most important thing is to have the support of the people around girls who study while pregnant, because that really makes things easiest.

49
00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:27.170
I was very lucky there because my parents met me halfway a lot, so I was basically at the faculty all the time and rarely missed anything.

50
00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:32.900
I'm glad that both Katarina and Ivana have their families' support.

51
00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:41.560
Without it, fulfilling all their daily obligations would probably be much harder, maybe even impossible.

52
00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:46.550
For a moment I wondered: what about support from the state?

53
00:05:46.550 --> 00:06:01.810
And then I remembered 2018 and the campaign to boost the birth rate in Serbia carried out by the Ministry of Information and Culture, as well as the slogans that won the contest back then.

54
00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:11.310
Love and a baby, the first thing we need. Give birth, don't postpone. Enough words, let the baby cry out.

55
00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:17.940
Okay, maybe it's better not to go in that direction, I'm afraid I'll annoy both you and myself.

56
00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:24.100
After all, this episode is about nice things, babies and their student moms.

57
00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:29.110
Heroines who fight every day for a better future for their children.

58
00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:34.770
It occurred to me to go back to the place where it all began.

59
00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:35.650
To the faculty.

60
00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:43.250
I wondered what kind of support students can expect from the faculty if they get pregnant during their studies.

61
00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:53.550
To get an answer to that question, I went to another person who decided to become a mom before finishing college.

62
00:06:53.770 --> 00:07:00.190
I am Kristina Mladenović, head of the teaching and student affairs service at the Faculty of Law of the University of Niš.

63
00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:13.770
The fact that Kristina also got pregnant during her studies helps her understand other girls, her young colleagues who find themselves in the same situation, and work in their best interest.

64
00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:26.220
Students who became pregnant during their studies have the right to submit a request that their rights and obligations be put on hold, students call it freezing the status.

65
00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.170
What does that mean?

66
00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:36.830
It means that the moment the request is submitted along with medical documentation, the student receives a decision by which her status is somehow frozen in time.

67
00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.550
That is, it stops where it was.

68
00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:45.540
In other words, every student who gets pregnant during her studies has the right to freeze her studies.

69
00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:55.250
If she decides to do so, her studies stay frozen during the pregnancy and maternity leave, which counts as a year after the birth.

70
00:07:55.870 --> 00:08:03.990
After maternity leave the child is considered grown enough for the nursery, so the student can return to the faculty.

71
00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:12.410
If for any reason the child needs special care, this freezing period can be extended.

72
00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:20.290
After the reason for the suspension ends, the student returns to the same status she had before submitting the request.

73
00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:24.710
That means she continues her studies on a state-funded place, without paying tuition.

74
00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:30.720
Of course, this applies only to those students who were on a state-funded place before the pregnancy.

75
00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:37.110
Those who paid tuition continue paying from where they stopped before the pregnancy.

76
00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:45.050
All pre-exam obligations that students fulfilled before the pregnancy remain valid after they return to the faculty.

77
00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:50.950
Well, I wouldn't call this some special support, but at least it's fair.

78
00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:56.850
But how does it actually look in practice? I went back to Ivana and Katarina.

79
00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:13.800
I knew a girl who was pregnant in her second year, and she told me that I have the right to graduate-student exam periods, so that is a relief I had and still have now as a parent and as a pregnant woman.

80
00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:31.000
Shortly before I got pregnant, it was on TV that we would be exempt from lectures, exercises and so on, which again I don't think should be the case, at least not at our medical school, because I can't treat people tomorrow whom I haven't seen, so I really didn't expect that.

81
00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:36.830
The period when Katarina was pregnant was a bit specific, though.

82
00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:44.140
If you've lived in Serbia for the past two years or are a big fan of this podcast, you can guess why.

83
00:09:44.520 --> 00:10:00.520
Well, at that moment it was during the blockades, that is, when the blockades and protests were in full swing, everything around that, so my pregnancy didn't affect my studies much then, because we weren't going to the faculty anyway.

84
00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:04.450
Katarina's daughter will soon be one year old.

85
00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:08.700
This young mom says she doesn't feel the need for any accommodations.

86
00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:14.650
Basically, I never explicitly told anyone at the faculty that I'd had a baby.

87
00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:18.680
Of course, I mentioned it later in conversation and so on.

88
00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:33.100
From other colleagues' experiences I know they were always open to it and accommodating, but I simply didn't need that kind of support from them, again, because of my family's support.

89
00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:42.990
Now that I know the faculty's legal obligations and am listening to Ivana's and Katarina's experiences, one more question was nagging me.

90
00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:50.230
A question that has little to do with documents, obligations, rights and similar formalities.

91
00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:53.520
A question about collegiality and prejudice.

92
00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:02.850
It's even interesting that in my eighth month I gave a seminar in front of a full lecture hall.

93
00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:16.960
I was wearing those maternity leggings, and just as I was going down the steps of the amphitheater I glanced at the professor, because it was important to me not to see some pointless look.

94
00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:21.910
I really didn't see one, and on their side it was fine with me.

95
00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:26.780
I even had some assistants who were accommodating.

96
00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.420
Do you remember where I first saw Ivana?

97
00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:32.090
That's right, on TikTok.

98
00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:38.100
In the world of social media, though, Ivana came across different comments.

99
00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:44.460
Comments like: how did you get pregnant so fast, who plans that normally at medical school.

100
00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:50.080
Maybe, but it is still completely pointless to say that, because we really wanted it.

101
00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:58.830
Despite the comments of people who obviously have nothing smarter to do, Ivana keeps filming for TikTok.

102
00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:02.860
And she does it, it seems to me, out of a very right conviction.

103
00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:13.930
I'm really only here to be an example to girls, to motivate them to work on themselves, whether they have a child or not, whether they got pregnant on purpose or by accident.

104
00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:21.720
It's important to me to have that inner feeling that I'm doing something good, and then those comments really don't hurt me.

105
00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:27.050
Like Ivana, Katarina mostly met with support at the faculty.

106
00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:36.620
Still, within a wider circle of acquaintances she would hear an opinion or two about her pregnancy that didn't match her plans.

107
00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:53.210
Some comments to the effect that they expected me to freeze a year now, stop working, not quit my studies entirely but just put it all on pause until the child grows up a bit.

108
00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:59.360
But I didn't consider it an offensive comment, people are simply curious.

109
00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:04.470
There are many challenges in studying and parenting at the same time.

110
00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:14.060
That is why I decided to ask my interviewees what advice they would give to girls in the same situation.

111
00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:26.120
That support from the people around you is very important, but even if you don't have it, you have that little being inside you or next to you, and you need to be a role model for him or her.

112
00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:30.590
Because look, what would I tell Kruna tomorrow if I had given up studying?

113
00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:33.530
What would I tell her tomorrow when she enrolls in college?

114
00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:35.980
I think I wouldn't be a good example.

115
00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:43.840
Well, first, to enjoy that period, both while they are mothers and while they study: as hard as it is, it is just as beautiful.

116
00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:49.010
Katarina's and Ivana's stories motivated me a lot.

117
00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:54.760
They showed me that everything is possible to achieve and do when you have the support of the people around you.

118
00:13:55.760 --> 00:14:04.960
Given everything that has been happening in our young lives lately, I wanted to end this episode with the following message.

119
00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:09.440
Support is important.

120
00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:14.970
Until the next listening.

121
00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:17.340
I am Milica Mihajlović.

122
00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:24.750
The editor of this podcast is Vladimir Radinović, and Dejan Tomka is in charge of sound.

123
00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.830
Production by Visions HQ.

124
00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:35.280
Thanks to the National Coalition for Decentralization, which contributed to the creation of this episode.
